ading creates no selected-control obligation.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u10\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Practicability qualifies SFC operational enhancements; contact guidance does not qualify the submission mandate.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Division attribution.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u12\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Commission attribution.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u13\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"End marker.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Footnote identifies the product categories associated with the scope clause.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Defines WINGS; does not establish a separate submission route.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u18\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dimensions\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The control concerns persons making applications or submissions for investment products administered by IPD, rather than all activities of an institution or all industry participants. It encompasses new-product and post-authorisation/registration submissions; specified reporting requests are to be integrated.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Footnote 1 supplies product categories. WINGS means Web-based INteGrated Service and hosts e-IP. The packet does not supply detailed classification rules for borderline products or communications.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u17\\\",\\\"u18\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Existing channels remain available during the extended parallel run. No post-transition exception or grandfathering is stated. 'where practicable' attaches to SFC review and enhancement, not to compulsory submission.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"'must' establishes the submission-route requirement. 'can also' makes annual-fee payment through e-IP an optional facility. Statements about future enhancements and integration do not themselves impose additional user duties.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The original 29 October 2024 endpoint is extended to 29 November 2024. Mandatory routing begins on 30 November 2024, inclusively. The packet does not specify dispatch-versus-receipt timing or treatment of follow-up material in existing cases.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The 8 July 2024 launch circular is referenced but absent. The listed external-authorities dependency contains no substantive text. Operational classification and legacy-case details cannot be resolved from those unavailable materials; the express transition date is not conditioned on their contents or completion of enhancements.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Does the referenced 8 July 2024 circular specify how follow-up submissions in cases opened before 30 November 2024 must be routed?\\\",\\n    \\\"Which event determines the submission date for material dispatched before, but received on or after, 30 November 2024?\\\",\\n    \\\"What classification guidance determines whether a borderline communication is an application or submission concerning an IPD-administered product?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"readings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\": [\\n        \\\"The control is evaluated for one identified application or submission, not for whole-institution compliance.\\\",\\n        \\\"Extending the parallel run extends its existing-channel acceptance through 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n        \\\"The supplied submission date is established under the applicable timing convention; this packet does not define that convention.\\\",\\n        \\\"Product and communication classification is supplied with professional judgment where needed.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"processing new product applications and post-authorisation/registration submissions to IPD.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u3\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u4\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u7\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"2 Web-based INteGrated Service.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u18\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"The express text supports one mandatory-route reading, without a sufficiently grounded rival that postpones the date, exempts existing cases or makes annual-fee payment compulsory. A covered submission made through an existing non-e-IP channel on 29 November 2024 falls within the extended parallel run; the same submission on 30 November falls within the compulsory e-IP control and fails that route check. A fee payment alone does not become a covered submission merely because e-IP can process it. The strongest uncertainty concerns operational treatment of legacy-case follow-ups and the event fixing the submission date.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The identified item is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD, interpreted with the product categories in footnote 1. Optional fee payment alone does not establish this classification.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"covered_submission\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The Gregorian date on which the identified application or submission is treated as submitted under the applicable timing convention. Dispatch-versus-receipt treatment is not specified in the packet.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"submission_date\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"date\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Gregorian calendar date\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The identified application or submission was submitted to IPD via e-IP.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"submitted_via_e_ip\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"\\n          }\\n        ],\\n        \\\"result\\\":\\\"submitted_via_e_ip\\\",\\n        \\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n        \\\"scope\\\":\\\"(and covered_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"r1\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\n        \\\"For a case initiated through an existing channel before the transition, is later correspondence itself a covered submission requiring e-IP?\\\",\\n        \\\"Does unavailable operational guidance distinguish attempted transmission from accepted receipt when determining the submission date?\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"Selected control: compulsory e-IP submission route from 30 November 2024